              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KslCx",
              "name": "Chose: a hard cap at the win",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: a hard cap at the window's free height (482 px, less 34 per edge), with the deck folding to one edge before the body is cut. The cut is a fade plus Show all, which says how much is left (\"2 min read\", \"11 rows\", \"5 steps\"). Expanding is always by hand, to 640 px wide and up to the work area's height; only there does the body scroll. State line and footer stay pinned, so Stop, Copy and Show less never move. Folding back: Show less, Esc, or a click on the orb. Rejected: auto-expanding long answers (covers your work without a reason); a scrolling capped card (scroll inside a 482 px overlay is fiddly and hides how much there is); a separate reader window for anything long (B12 keeps the reader for after the card has gone). Question for the owner: should expanding also pause the reading timer for every other Done card in the deck, or only this one?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "S8ZtF",
          "name": "B7  Motion you can see",
          "fill": "#121522",
          "content": "B7  Motion you can see",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 32,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "SkcYt",
          "name": "Today's 120/160/200 ms fades",
          "fill": "#3A3F4D",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1600,
          "content": "Today's 120/160/200 ms fades are over before the eye finds them, so a card seems to appear from nowhere. Motion should say where a thing came from and where it went: out of the orb, back into the orb, forward from the deck. Frames below are the window's bottom-right corner at 1:3 scale; times are from the trigger.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$font-text",
          "fontSize": 17,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
