              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "DJS5O",
              "name": "Chose: Open the answer opens",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: Open the answer opens the run record in the reader, so it works after the card has faded and after a restart. Finished is green (it's Done), ENDED is grey (you stopped it, nothing failed), and ENDED offers Open what I have and Carry on. Rejected: reopening the card (it has a reading time and a deck slot, wrong for something you came back to); red for Stop (red is failure only). Question for the owner: the reader is a normal window you opened, so it can take focus when clicked. Is that the one allowed exception, like the typing box?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
