        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "aueO3",
          "name": "Note · B13",
          "width": 1600,
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "cornerRadius": 12,
          "stroke": "#2357C9",
          "strokeWidth": {
            "left": 3
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            16,
            20
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ucyS6",
              "name": "Note · B13",
              "fill": "#2357C9",
              "content": "Note · B13",
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "E1GVn",
              "name": "Chose: one new block, Tree r",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: one new block, Tree row (28 px, 18 px per level), reused for file search, downloads and cleanup. Folders start collapsed except the one that answers the question; long names are cut in the middle so the extension survives; \"+ N more\" opens in place. Selecting a row puts its path in the footer with Open and Show in folder. The reader shows everything and is the only place with keyboard navigation. Rejected: a flat list with paths (unreadable past ten items); checkboxes for bulk actions (bulk delete or move must go through their own Needs your OK card, so selection that implies action is a trap). Question for the owner: should the tree remember which folders you opened for the same folder next time?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "W0wQu",
          "name": "Note · B14",
          "width": 1600,
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "cornerRadius": 12,
          "stroke": "#2357C9",
          "strokeWidth": {
            "left": 3
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            16,
            20
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "x6kzML",
              "name": "Note · B14",
              "fill": "#2357C9",
              "content": "Note · B14",
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PbjNO",
              "name": "Chose: the orb carries a run",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: the orb carries a running timer as a thin arc plus a small time pill on the screen side; an edge when a card is in front; a row under \"Running\" in the stack. Due is unchanged (solid, accent ring, no close), and +5 min puts the arc back at 5:00. Rejected: a Working card for timers (it says \"Swift is busy\" when Swift isn't); a number inside the orb (too small at 36 px and fights the mic states); amber for the last minute (amber means an OK, nothing else). Question for the owner: with two timers running, is \"4:12 · 2\" on the pill enough, or should the arc split?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "anGuV",
          "name": "Note · B4 shapes",
          "width": 1600,
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "cornerRadius": 12,
          "stroke": "#2357C9",
          "strokeWidth": {
            "left": 3
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            16,
            20
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "twzdk",
              "name": "Note · B4 shapes",
              "fill": "#2357C9",
              "content": "Note · B4 shapes",
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "WlK66",
              "name": "Chose: each shape is built f",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: each shape is built from layout, the same way as compare. The worker's part sits behind the grey bar with its caption (\"Grouped by…\", \"Compared by…\", \"Outlined by…\"), the Worker's pick is grey, the byline is just \"Swift\", and a document preview is rendered by Swift from the file, with the worker only naming the page and passage. When a shape doesn't fit (too many series, too wide a map), Swift shows plain text and says why in one grey line. Rejected: line and pie charts (layout can't place points or labels reliably, and they're harder to read aloud); worker-coloured highlights (only Swift picks colours). Question for the owner: should the chart's Worker's pick use the grey bar fill as drawn, or a grey outline so that every bar keeps the same weight?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
