        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "AiRs7",
          "name": "Note · B3",
          "width": 1600,
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "cornerRadius": 12,
          "stroke": "#2357C9",
          "strokeWidth": {
            "left": 3
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            16,
            20
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "uTe5W",
              "name": "Note · B3",
              "fill": "#2357C9",
              "content": "Note · B3",
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "kAfsI",
              "name": "Chose: keep the seven treatm",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: keep the seven treatments and prove them at every size. Each state differs in at least two ways that survive grayscale: the band (OK only), ring weight (Waiting 5 px, Due 5 px on a solid surface), the mark's shape (spinner, check, shield, tag, square, exclamation, bell), and always the word. Edges carry the mark and the word in the state's text colour; badges carry the mark on the orb. Rejected: colour-only edges (fail the grayscale test); a pulsing Waiting card (motion as the only difference, and it breaks reduced motion). Question for the owner: Waiting for you and Due both use the accent ring. They differ by surface (glass vs solid), tag vs bell, and the close button. Is that enough, or should Due's ring be 3 px?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "hkrSq",
          "name": "Note · ADR-019 §8",
          "width": 1600,
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "cornerRadius": 12,
          "stroke": "#2357C9",
          "strokeWidth": {
            "left": 3
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            16,
            20
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Pumhw",
              "name": "Note · ADR-019 §8",
              "fill": "#2357C9",
              "content": "Note · ADR-019 §8",
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "t3hhjM",
              "name": "Chose: (1) every confirm and",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: (1) every confirm and question carries an origin line. The approval card leads with the worker's sentence behind the grey bar, and Swift's facts box (runs in, will run, removes) carries what matters. (2) Times are relative while a run is on screen: m:ss running, \"just now\", \"N min ago\". Clock times live in the reader. (3) Failed has no reading bar and keeps partial results with \"Try again from step N\". (4) A problem nobody asked about is still Failed, with Swift's origin on the left. (5) At right anchors the speaking pill grows away from the corner and the orb's centre never moves. (6) The compact confirm comes first, then the deck folds to one edge; the card never scrolls. Rejected: a separate \"warning\" card for unrequested problems (one more treatment to learn, and amber would be tempting). Question for the owner: should a Failed card that moved to the stack after 10 minutes still count on the orb's badge?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "mYxbj",
      "x": 26800,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Halo · B8 · Where Halo could go (exploration)",
      "width": 4600,
      "fill": "#E8EBF2",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 56,
      "padding": 72,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "wywxx",
          "name": "Header",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "gap": 56,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "CWPD0",
              "name": "Title",
              "width": 1200,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "MbXWz",
                  "name": "Halo · B8 · Board 8 · Explor",
                  "fill": "#2357C9",
                  "content": "Halo · B8 · Board 8 · Exploration, all proposal",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "O8HljV",
                  "name": "Where Halo could go",
                  "fill": "#121522",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Where Halo could go",
                  "lineHeight": 1.1,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-display",
                  "fontSize": 52,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "oDKGV",
                  "name": "Not a feature wish list. Thi",
                  "fill": "#262B3A",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Not a feature wish list. This board starts from what owners are trying to do, finds where Halo gets in the way or falls short, and keeps only ideas with a clear benefit that fit one anatomy, seven states and the block catalog. Each idea is marked as a refinement of something that exists or a genuinely new feature, and scored before anything is drawn.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 20,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "dnWkg",
              "name": "How ideas were judged",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "padding": [
                24,
                0,
                0,
                0
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "H0fP1N",
                  "name": "How ideas were judged",
                  "fill": "#121522",
                  "content": "How ideas were judged",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "UQkn5",
                  "name": "• Value: does it remove a re",
                  "fill": "#3A3F4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Value: does it remove a real step, a real worry or a real miss for the owner?",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "tTxA1",
                  "name": "• Usability: can the owner p",
                  "fill": "#3A3F4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Usability: can the owner predict it, notice it and undo it without learning anything new?",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "i69iqP",
                  "name": "• Fit: does it use Halo's an",
                  "fill": "#3A3F4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Fit: does it use Halo's anatomy, states, blocks and verbs, and keep amber, red and focus rules intact?",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "eHXJv",
                  "name": "• Cost: S (overlay only), M ",
                  "fill": "#3A3F4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Cost: S (overlay only), M (overlay plus run records or one OS hook), L (new subsystem).",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "EuVtN",
                  "name": "• Verdict: Do next · Explore",
                  "fill": "#3A3F4D",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Verdict: Do next · Explore (needs a test with the owner) · Park (good, not now) · Reject.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-text",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
