            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "W9BukT",
              "name": "What I chose: ideas that clo",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "What I chose: ideas that close a gap in one of six owner jobs and use only existing anatomy. Two new blocks (Caveat, Phrases), one new edge (Pinned), one new origin (\"While you were in your call\", the existing away origin) and one settings page. Nine are Do next. The Explore four need a test with the owner because they're anticipatory: helpful when right, intrusive when wrong. What I rejected: a chat-history sidebar (takes focus and space, and turns runs into a log), an avatar (decoration), custom state colours (breaks amber and red), anything that acts unasked. What I didn't check: whether Windows exposes \"in a call\" and \"sharing screen\" reliably enough for A3 without per-app hooks. That is the one technical risk on this board. Question for the owner: is one pin enough, or do you keep two things in view (a number and a step) often enough to justify two?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
