            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "gMNnL",
              "name": "Chose: draw every built surf",
              "fill": "#262B3A",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Chose: draw every built surface from Halo's parts rather than leave them as one-offs. Three new components (State · Notice, Stack · Row, Stack · Pile) and no new colours. The stack grows out of Halo's own pile, its rows follow the code's pane, and the B14 and A1 panels now use it. Notices and problems are cards about Swift itself, so they're solid and carry a neutral notice line; only a stopped engine is red, and only an OK is amber, including the \"say approve again\" line. The text box keeps the one keyboard exception and spells out what Enter does in each mode. Rejected: a separate design for system messages (toasts) — Swift already has one place it speaks from, the orb. Not covered: Settings itself (the tray's Settings opens config.yaml today, so there's no screen to design yet), and the Swift window (ADR-018), which doesn't exist yet. Questions for the owner: should \"Swift is ready\" show on every start or only after an update or crash? And should the stack's \"Earlier today\" section (A1) ship with the list, or wait?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-text",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
